arsenal.guide.basics=Basics
arsenal.guide.basics.1=Use (right-click / tap) fires. Hold for full-auto.
arsenal.guide.basics.2=Sneak aims down sights (toggle in settings). Double-tap Sneak reloads.
arsenal.guide.basics.3=Look straight up and Use to open the weapon menu: attachments, ammo, fire mode, camo.
arsenal.guide.basics.4=Jump + Sneak in mid-air switches fire mode. Jump while scoped holds your breath.
arsenal.guide.basics.5=Hit something with a gun in hand for a buttstroke.
arsenal.guide.basics.6=HUD 2.0 shows ammo, plates, health, compass and scores. Switch to classic in HUD settings.
arsenal.guide.basics.7=Weapons are crafted at the Weapon Bench; ammo at the Ammo Press.
arsenal.guide.basics.8=Run /scriptevent arsenal:calib to fine-tune where the gun sits in first person.
arsenal.guide.combat=Combat
arsenal.guide.combat.1=Headshots deal extra damage; helmets reduce it. Legs take less.
arsenal.guide.combat.2=Bullets pierce thin blocks. Sniper fire at long range drifts with the wind.
arsenal.guide.combat.3=Near misses suppress you: the screen edges darken and your spread grows.
arsenal.guide.combat.4=Melee weapons: backstabs deal huge damage. Hold Use then release for a heavy lunge.
arsenal.guide.combat.5=Sneak + Use throws the combat knife or fires the spring knife's blade.
arsenal.guide.combat.6=The Breaching Axe smashes doors, trapdoors and fences in one hit.
arsenal.guide.combat.7=Energy weapons, drones and turrets stop working under EMP.
arsenal.guide.combat.8=Grenades: frag, smoke, flash, gas, EMP, cluster, decoy, snap - check the codex.
arsenal.guide.enemies=Enemies
arsenal.guide.enemies.1=Raiders roam plains and deserts at night. Iron Legion machines guard the mountains. The Hollow lurk underground.
arsenal.guide.enemies.2=Enemies take cover, flank, heal each other and throw grenades.
arsenal.guide.enemies.3=Drones spot you for their squad - shoot them down or use EMP.
arsenal.guide.enemies.4=Shield troopers block bullets from the front: flank or aim at their legs.
arsenal.guide.enemies.5=Bloaters swell up and explode when close. Keep your distance.
arsenal.guide.enemies.6=Decoy grenades lure enemies away from your position.
arsenal.guide.enemies.7=Enemy AI difficulty can be changed in World Settings (2.0).
arsenal.guide.gear=Armor & Gear
arsenal.guide.gear.1=Body armor holds armor plates. Each plate soaks 10 damage before your health.
arsenal.guide.gear.2=Use an Armor Plate item to insert one (takes a moment).
arsenal.guide.gear.3=Bandages and medkits stop bleeding; medkits heal over time. Adrenaline speeds you up.
arsenal.guide.gear.4=Place turrets, shields, claymores and stations on the top face of a block.
arsenal.guide.gear.5=Sneak-interact with your own deployable to pick it up.
arsenal.guide.gear.6=Mount emplacements and aim with your view; hold Jump to fire.
arsenal.guide.gear.7=The buggy and APC need fuel canisters; steel ingots repair vehicles.
arsenal.guide.gear.8=Night vision goggles switch on in the dark (toggle in the Field Manual).
arsenal.guide.mobile=Phones & Tablets
arsenal.guide.mobile.1=Set Trigger to 'tap' so one tap starts full-auto and the next stops it.
arsenal.guide.mobile.2=HUD position 'Auto' raises the ammo panel above the touch buttons.
arsenal.guide.mobile.3=Aim assist and auto-fire help against mobs (off by default).
arsenal.guide.mobile.4=Look straight up and tap Use to open the weapon menu.
arsenal.guide.mobile.5=Emplacement fire uses the Jump button; in tap mode each press toggles fire.
arsenal.guide.mobile.6=Lower 'Effects quality' if the game stutters.
arsenal.guide.mobile.7=Scope overlays and HUD 2.0 need the resource pack enabled.
arsenal.guide.modes=Game Modes
arsenal.guide.modes.1=Operators build arenas with the Arena Tool: two corners, spawns, and hills for King of the Hill.
arsenal.guide.modes.2=Free-for-All, Team Deathmatch, Gun Game, Horde and King of the Hill are available.
arsenal.guide.modes.3=Join from the Field Manual > Game Modes during the lobby countdown.
arsenal.guide.modes.4=Your inventory and position are stored and returned after the match - even after a restart.
arsenal.guide.modes.5=You can't die in a match: you respawn after a few seconds.
arsenal.guide.modes.6=Horde: survive 20 waves of Hollow together, with bosses every 5 waves.
arsenal.guide.modes.7=Gun Game: every kill swaps your gun; win with the knife.
arsenal.guide.progress=Progression
arsenal.guide.progress.1=Weapons gain XP from hits and kills and level up to 40.
arsenal.guide.progress.2=Weapon levels unlock camos; attachment tiers need weapon levels (world setting).
arsenal.guide.progress.3=Your rank (1-50) rises with every kill, challenge and match.
arsenal.guide.progress.4=Three daily and three weekly challenges rotate automatically.
arsenal.guide.progress.5=Credits come from kills, clears, waves and challenges.
arsenal.guide.progress.6=The black market (rank 5+) sells legendary gear that changes daily.
arsenal.guide.progress.7=Killstreaks: open the Streak Terminal to call in recon, supply drops, airstrikes and more.
arsenal.guide.trouble=Troubleshooting
arsenal.guide.trouble.1=No HUD panels? Make sure both packs are active, or switch HUD style to Classic.
arsenal.guide.trouble.2=Gun sits oddly in first person? Run /scriptevent arsenal:calib.
arsenal.guide.trouble.3=Before removing the add-on, run /scriptevent arsenal:normalize to restore weapon IDs.
arsenal.guide.trouble.4=Run /scriptevent arsenal:report and share the result when reporting a bug.
arsenal.guide.trouble.5=Items from a match not returned? Rejoin near the arena; they come back automatically.
arsenal.guide.trouble.6=Too many enemies? Turn factions off or lower structure density in World Settings (2.0).
arsenal.guide.trouble.7=Performance: enemy thinking is budgeted; reduce view distance if needed.
arsenal.guide.world=World
arsenal.guide.world.1=Camps, outposts, bunkers, labs, crash sites, ports and nests appear as you explore.
arsenal.guide.world.2=Clear a structure's garrison for a bonus; its chests hold loot by tier.
arsenal.guide.world.3=Quartermasters sell weapons, ammo and gear for credits.
arsenal.guide.world.4=Bosses are summoned with the Warlord's Banner and the Legion Core.
arsenal.guide.world.5=Bosses telegraph big attacks - watch for markers and warnings.
arsenal.guide.world.6=Structure density can be set to off, low, normal or high.
arsenal.guide.world.7=Hollow nests spawn mutants at night.
